---
portal:
  portal:
    # dev decrypts a Pipeline's `secretRef` with SOPS and an age identity (T-0935, CC-06,
    # ADR-N-012). One node, one tenant: OpenBao's server and its Kubernetes auth method buy
    # nothing here and cost ~256 MB on a 16 GB box, and the multi-tenant installations that
    # need it configure `JC_PORTAL_OPENBAO_ADDR` instead — never both.
    #
    # The Secret is operator-supplied and created once, from the identity kept in `.secrets/`:
    #
    #   kubectl -n dev create secret generic portal-age-identity \
    #     --from-file=keys.txt=.secrets/age-dev.key
    #
    # Its public recipient is what encrypts the `*.enc.yaml` files of the configuration
    # repository the Portal stages. Without the Secret the mount is empty and every reference
    # is refused with "the age identity is unreadable", which is the same fail-closed answer.
    sopsAgeSecret: portal-age-identity
    rawValues:
      env:
        # Dev only (T-6083, owner 2026-10-29): the demo approvers sign in with a password alone
        # (approverMfa false, T-5776), so the decision doors (approve, reject, revoke, people)
        # stop asking for a one-time code here. smartcity reuses dev's values profile, which is
        # why this sits in dev's environment and not in development-values; smartcity and the
        # production profile keep AUT-2 (the Portal's default; only "false" turns it off).
        JC_PORTAL_DECISIONS_NEED_SECOND_FACTOR: "false"
  # No relay yet (T-3309): App mail lands in the in-cluster catcher, where a person reads it with
  # `kubectl -n dev port-forward svc/mail-catcher 8025` and the e2e reads `/api/v1/messages`
  # (T-3583). Naming the relay later is `portal-mail-relay` and this switched off.
  mail-catcher:
    enabled: true
